BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Applying Your Transferable Skills
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260619T140000
UID:6a0620b0490f176f7dd5398c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Once you have identified your transferable skills\, the next s
 tep is learning how to communicate them effectively. In this hands-on work
 shop\, participants will learn how to transform past experiences into impa
 ct-driven resume bullet points and compelling cover letter content. By the
  end of the session\, you will have practical tools to position your exper
 ience clearly and strategically for your target roles.\nThis program is pa
 rt of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously supported by our
  lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors Fidelity Canad
 a\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nWilliam and Non
 a Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careerc
 oach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0620b0490f176f7dd5398c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Managing Your Money in Challenging Times
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T150000
UID:69d962f42866a5b48847c868@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This workshop helps participants understand different types of
  debt and how to manage them effectively. Topics include budgeting\, prior
 itizing debt payments\, understanding interest\, and exploring options for
  reducing or paying off debt. The session is facilitated by a Financial Em
 powerment staff member from North York Community House and is practical\, 
 easy to follow\, and tailored to the needs of individuals and families in 
 Ontario.
LOCATION:Downsview\, Auditorium (Lower level)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d962f42866a5b48847c868
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
