BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python III
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T190000
UID:6a1e0e63703c3363002b9cee@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this follow up course we will be designing and implementing
  some simple Object Oriented Programming data structures.\nPython is an op
 en source programming language that is used for creating web applications\
 , web content\, mathematics and system scripting. In this follow up course
  we will really start to stretch our legs in Python\, designing and implem
 enting some simple Object Oriented Programming data structures. Key takeaw
 ays will include a working knowledge of Python classes and objects.\nThis 
 class is for beginners but assumes you have a basic understanding of Pytho
 n or have attended Coding with Python I and II.\nPrior to the class\, part
 icipants will need to download and install Python and VS Code onto their p
 ersonal computers (installation guides provided after registration).\nRegi
 stration is limited and specific instructions including information about 
 software installation will be provided.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nT
 he personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Li
 brary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d).
  The information will only be used for event and program registration\, de
 livery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your inform
 ation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-39
 7-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, 2nd Floor Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1e0e63703c3363002b9cee
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
