BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Job Search Cheat Codes: The New Search Skills No One Taught You
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T180000
UID:69fca95b278f7c2f008bab27@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Finding a job today can feel like searching for a needle in a 
 haystack. With endless postings\, automated applications\, and recruiters 
 who seem impossible to reach\, many young professionals end up frustrated\
 , applying to roles without strategy or direction. Yet\, there’s a hidde
 n layer of the job market: recruiters\, staffing agencies\, and unadvertis
 ed opportunities\, that most people never learn how to access. This intera
 ctive workshop is designed to change that. You’ll learn how to harness n
 ew search techniques\, optimize online platforms like Google and LinkedIn\
 , and create personalized outreach that actually gets noticed. The ultimat
 e goal? To give you control over your job search\, shifting from passive a
 pplications to proactive\, confident\, and bold opportunity-finding.\nThis
  program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Residence and is generously su
 pported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation along with supporting donors 
 Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter and\nW
 illiam and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more information\, please visit\n
 tpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fca95b278f7c2f008bab27
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
