BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Art by Kazui Ikenshi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260601T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260630T090000
UID:6a24322a7b73be6a1b1ab8f4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of June\, works by artist Kazui Ikenishi
  are on display at Bloor Gladstone Library in an exhibit.\nKazui Ikenishi 
 is an abstract painter born and raised in Japan\, now based in Toronto\, C
 anada. A self-taught artist\, she began painting in September 2023 and qu
 ickly developed a passion for vibrant\, expressive compositions. Working p
 rimarily with acrylic paint\, she embraces bold colors and dynamic forms 
 in her artwork. Her creative process is deeply intuitive\, often drawing i
 nspiration from her own sketches and spontaneous explorations on the\ncanv
 as.\nKazui's works explores spontaneity\, movement\, and connection throu
 gh bold colors and fluid forms. Starting with rough underdrawing on a read
 ymade canvas\, she let's intuition guide the composition.  Using opaque a
 crylics\, she creates a rhythm - flowly like music- where shapes interact 
 freely\, much like an improvisational melody.  The overlapping colors and
  organic forms symbolize how elements in life connect.  She balances stru
 cture and spontianeity\, allowing each piece to evolve naturally.\nThe exh
 ibit can be viewed during Bloor/Gladstone branch's open hours. Please che
 ck the\nBloor/Gladstone branch\npage before you visit.\nFree. All are welc
 ome.\nImage credit: Kazui Ikenshi\; Infinite Connection\; Medium: Acrylic
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a24322a7b73be6a1b1ab8f4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
