BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rob Godwin: Project Apollo
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260704T160000
UID:6a206d6fc7d3cd58005dcd63@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a talk with Rob Godwin\, author and Research Direc
 tor at General Astronautics Research Corporation. Learn about the history 
 of the Apollo program\, the journey to get there\, and Godwin's involvemen
 t with the astronauts who walked on the moon!\nGodwin's talk will be follo
 wed by a live Q&A with the audience. Copies of his books will be available
  for sale and signing at the event.\nHosted by the Merril Collection of Sc
 ience Fiction\, Speculation and Fantasy.\nRob Godwin is the award-winning 
 author of over 100 books on space. He is also the founder of Apogee Books\
 , an imprint of Collector's Guide Publishing. Launched in 1998\, the first
  Apogee title was "Apollo 8 The NASA Mission Reports". It was published at
  the personal request of astronaut Buzz Aldrin. Godwin was also the Space 
 Curator at the Canadian Air & Space Museum. He is a lifetime member of the
  both the National Space Society and the Space Frontier Foundation and a m
 ember of the International Astronautical Federation and American Astronaut
 ical Society History Committees.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a206d6fc7d3cd58005dcd63
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
