DESCRIPTION:The Brentwood Branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variet
 y of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the n
 atural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differe
 nt species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\n
 Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistration
  is required and will open June 20th.\nThe tour will start and end at the 
 Brentwood Branch Community Room and will be guided by the City of Toronto 
 Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the rou
 te. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gl
 oves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program
  takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, reg
 istrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part of
  TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toron
 to Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe
