BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Prose Poem Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T200000
UID:6a2066b4e13d3b4603b6501a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever wondered what the difference between prose and a
  poem is? What is prose at all\, really? In this workshop\, beginners and 
 advanced writers alike will gather to discuss and create around the trendi
 ng phenomenon of the prose poem. With the inclusion of examples from othe
 r Toronto poets\, we hope to make this a generative space for writers acr
 oss genre by prying into this unique\, refreshing hybrid form.\n​This wo
 rkshop is led by Toronto poet\, Sanna Wani\, author of\nMy Grief\, the Sun
 : Poems\nand\nLantern: Poems\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
