DESCRIPTION:The Thorncliffe branch and its neighbourhood is home to a vari
 ety of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the
  natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize diffe
 rent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.
 \nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nRegistrati
 on is required – please register online or call the branch for assistan
 ce.\nThe tour will start and end at the Thorncliffe branch\, program room
  and will be guided by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There ma
 y be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare a
 ccordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscree
 n\, water\, comfortable shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In
  the event of severe inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of a
 n alternative date.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informat
 ion on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Publ
 ic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information wil
 l only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluatio
 n. Questions about how the library handles your information can be directe
 d to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge S
 treet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
